   "source": [
    "# Pricing and Hedging of European Options\n",
    "Anas KHAYAR\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from math import comb\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Cox–Ross–Rubinstein model (compact)\n",
    "Discrete time: $t_0=0<\dots<t_N=T$, $\delta=T/N$.\n",
    "Riskless asset: $(1+r_N)^i$ at time $t_i$.\n",
    "Risky asset: $S^{(N)}_{t_i}=T^{(N)}_i S^{(N)}_{t_{i-1}}$, with $T^{(N)}_i\in\{1+h_N,1+b_N\}$.\n",
    "Discounted price: $\\tilde S^{(N)}_{t_i}=S^{(N)}_{t_i}/(1+r_N)^i$.\n",
    "Risk-neutral probability $Q$ makes $(\\tilde S^{(N)}_{t_i})_i$ a martingale.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "$$q_N=\\frac{r_N-b_N}{h_N-b_N}$$\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "$$Prix^{(N)}=\\frac{1}{(1+r_N)^N}\\sum_{k=0}^N\\binom{N}{k}q_N^k(1-q_N)^{N-k}\\,f\\big(s(1+h_N)^k(1+b_N)^{N-k}\\big)$$\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import math\n",
    "\n",
    "def price1(N, rN, hN, bN, s, f):\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Return the binomial-model price: Prix^{(N)} = (1/(1+rN)^N) E_Q[f(S_T)].\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    qn = (rN - bN) / (hN - bN)\n",
    "    total = 0.0\n",
    "    for k in range(N+1):\n",
    "        ST = s * (1+hN)**k * (1+bN)**(N-k)\n",
    "        proba = math.comb(N,k) * qn**k * (1-qn)**(N-k)\n",
    "        total += proba * f(ST)\n",
    "    return total / (1 + rN) ** N\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "20.078658207286075"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 19,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "f = lambda x: max(x - 100, 0)\n",
    "price1(20, 0.01, 0.05, -0.05, 100, f)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def price2(N, rN, hN, bN, s, f):\n",
    "    qN = (rN - bN) / (hN - bN)\n",
    "    prices = np.zeros(N+1)\n",
    "    for k in range(N+1):\n",
    "        prices[k] = s * (1+hN)**k * (1+bN)**(N-k)\n",
    "    V = [f(x) for x in prices]\n",
    "    for k in range(N-1, -1, -1):\n",
    "        for i in range(k+1):\n",
    "            V[i] = (1/(1+rN))*(qN * V[i+1] + (1-qN)*V[i])\n",
    "    return V\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Hedging — compact formulas\n",
    "At node with asset price $x$ and next-step values $v_k((1+h_N)x)=V_{up}$, $v_k((1+b_N)x)=V_{down}$:\n",
    "$$\\alpha_{k-1}(x)=\\frac{V_{up}-V_{down}}{x(h_N-b_N)}\\qquad\\text{(Delta)}$$\n",
    "$$\\beta_{k-1}(x)=\\frac{(1+h_N)V_{down}-(1+b_N)V_{up}}{(1+r_N)^k(h_N-b_N)}$$\n",
    "Special case $v_N=f$:\n",
    "$$\\alpha_{N-1}(x)=\\frac{f((1+h_N)x)-f((1+b_N)x)}{x(h_N-b_N)}$$\n",
    "$$\\beta_{N-1}(x)=\\frac{(1+h_N)f((1+b_N)x)-(1+b_N)f((1+h_N)x)}{(1+r_N)^N(h_N-b_N)}$$\n",
    "Mapping to array indices for coding: up child = V[j+1], down child = V[j].\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 51,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def hedge(N, rN, hN, bN, s, f):\n",
    "    alpha = []\n",
    "    beta = []\n",
    "    for k in range(1, N + 1):\n",
    "        alpha_k = []\n",
    "        beta_k = []\n",
    "        for j in range(k):\n",
    "            x = s * (1 + hN)**j * (1 + bN)**(k - 1 - j)\n",
    "            v_up   = price2(N - k, rN, hN, bN, (1 + hN) * x, f)[0]\n",
    "            v_down = price2(N - k, rN, hN, bN, (1 + bN) * x, f)[0]\n",
    "            a = (v_up - v_down) / (x * (hN - bN))\n",
    "            b = ((1 + hN) * v_down - (1 + bN) * v_up) / ((1 + rN)**k * (hN - bN))\n",
    "            alpha_k.append(a)\n",
    "            beta_k.append(b)\n",
    "        alpha.append(alpha_k)\n",
    "        beta.append(beta_k)\n",
    "    return alpha, beta\n"
   ]
  },
  {
